        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on scope, zones, and initial move sequence for the relocation project.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 538335,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, let's kick off the Warehouse Heavy-Goods Relocation project. The main goal is to move bulky items while improving our safety standards. First up is T1: mapping our current layout. I've started a draft in A1. Which zones should we prioritize for the first phase to minimize disruption to daily shipments?",
            "mentions": [
              373940,
              221215,
              216869,
              62106
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 373940,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Good start. I'd suggest Zones C and D. They're consistently congested and moving them would clear a major access route. It also gives us a good mix of item types to test our process. I've added my notes on the current layout to A1.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 216869,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "What about Zone F? It has a lot of the big stuff.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 221215,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Zone F is tricky, it's right next to the main outbound loading bay. Moving that first could cause major delays if we run into any issues. I think C and D are a safer bet to start with.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 538335,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "I agree. Let's avoid Zone F for now. The risk of impacting outbound schedules is too high. So, are we all aligned on starting with Zones C and D for the first phase?",
            "mentions": [
              373940,
              221215,
              216869,
              62106
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 373940,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Yes, C and D are confirmed. I'll mark this in A1.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
